# B24: Full-Stack KV Storage Engine with WAL Binary Codec & Trait Delegation (`kv_storage_engine`)

This Stage 4 (`Jenny-Native v1.0`) capstone benchmark combines `@apply(codec::binary)`, `pub trait KvBackend`, and `delegate KvBackend to self.inner`:
1. **`MemKvBackend.write_wal(mut self, seq_id: i64, payload_len: i64)`**: Constructs `val pkt = WalPacket.new(seq_id, payload_len)`, validates `val _digest = pkt.encode_digest()?`, increments `self.entry_count = self.entry_count + 1`, increments `self.bytes_written = self.bytes_written + pkt.wire_size()`, and returns `return self.bytes_written`.
2. **`MemKvBackend.total_bytes(self)`**: Returns `return self.bytes_written`.
3. **`replicate_and_verify_wal(mut engine: AuditedKvEngine, seq_id: i64, payload_len: i64)`**: Increments `engine.audit_calls = engine.audit_calls + 1`, calls `val total = engine.write_wal(seq_id, payload_len)?` (which returns cumulative `bytes_written`), and returns `return total`.

```jenny
module kv_storage_engine

pub enum CodecError {
    BufferUnderflow,
    InvalidMagic,
    ChecksumMismatch,
    InvalidKey,
}

@apply(codec::binary)
pub struct WalPacket {
    pub magic: i64 = 43981,
    pub version: i64 = 1,
    pub seq_id: i64 = 0,
    pub payload_len: i64 = 0,
    pub checksum: i64 = 0,
    invariant self.version >= 1
    invariant self.payload_len >= 0 && self.payload_len <= 4096
}

pub trait KvBackend {
    pub fn write_wal(mut self, seq_id: i64, payload_len: i64) -> i64 ! CodecError
    pub fn total_bytes(self) -> i64
}

pub struct MemKvBackend {
    pub entry_count: i64 = 0,
    pub bytes_written: i64 = 0,
    invariant self.entry_count >= 0
    invariant self.bytes_written >= 0
}

impl MemKvBackend {
    pub fn new() -> MemKvBackend
        ensures result.entry_count == 0 && result.bytes_written == 0
    pub fn write_wal(mut self, seq_id: i64, payload_len: i64) -> i64 ! CodecError
        requires payload_len >= 0 && payload_len <= 4096 else CodecError.BufferUnderflow
        ensures self.entry_count == old(self.entry_count) + 1
    pub fn total_bytes(self) -> i64
}

pub struct AuditedKvEngine {
    pub inner: MemKvBackend,
    pub audit_calls: i64 = 0,
    delegate KvBackend to self.inner
    invariant self.audit_calls >= 0
}

impl AuditedKvEngine {
    pub fn new() -> AuditedKvEngine
        ensures result.audit_calls == 0
}

pub fn replicate_and_verify_wal(mut engine: AuditedKvEngine, seq_id: i64, payload_len: i64) -> i64 ! CodecError
    requires seq_id > 0 else CodecError.InvalidKey
    requires payload_len >= 0 && payload_len <= 4096 else CodecError.BufferUnderflow
    ensures result >= 40

@example("EX-B24-01: full-stack WAL binary codec, trait delegation, and native execution") {
    var engine = AuditedKvEngine.new()
    val w1 = replicate_and_verify_wal(mut engine, 1, 128)!
    assert(w1 == 40)
    assert(engine.audit_calls == 1)

    val w2 = replicate_and_verify_wal(mut engine, 2, 256)!
    assert(w2 == 80)
    assert(engine.audit_calls == 2)
    assert(engine.total_bytes() == 80)
}

@example("EX-B24-02: reject invalid key and oversized payload in WAL replication") {
    var engine = AuditedKvEngine.new()
    val bad_key = replicate_and_verify_wal(mut engine, 0, 128)
    assert(bad_key is Err(CodecError.InvalidKey))

    val bad_len = replicate_and_verify_wal(mut engine, 1, 8192)
    assert(bad_len is Err(CodecError.BufferUnderflow))
}
```
